Description: fdrv/usb: bound rx aggregate lengths to the received buffer
 Require a 4-byte header before reading the type byte. Compute copy and
 advance lengths in u32 and reject a firmware length that does not fit
 the bytes actually received, on the prealloc and skb paths and on the
 load-fw rx path. Zero-pad config messages and clamp param_len to the
 copied payload. Stop a reassembly fragment that would write past the
 allocated buffer. Free each load-fw data copy instead of leaking it
 across aggregate iterations.
Author: N Oliver <3945917+PixnBits@users.noreply.github.com>
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-26
